comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T11:04:30.930Z","harness:claude-code","Reproduction, identical fixture built twice at tree 9da5886cc with dist built from it.\n\nSetup in both runs (mirrors scripts/release/token-budget-gate.mjs runCli): isolated PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH, PM_NO_TELEMETRY=1, PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1, PM_TELEMETRY_OTEL_DISABLED=1, PM_TELEMETRY_PROMPT=0, PM_AUTHOR=token-budget-gate; then init --defaults, install audit --project, then 12 create calls.\n\n  Run A, host environment inherited (a Claude Code session):\n    pm health --check-only  ->  1,066 bytes\n    warnings: provenance_resolver_zero_success:claude-code:model:claude_session_file:12\n              provenance_resolver_zero_success:claude-code:version:claude_session_file:12\n    findings severity: advisory, check: storage\n\n  Run B, identical except the harness signal variables are unset\n  (CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION,\n   CLAUDE_CODE_BRIDGE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH, CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_SOCKET,\n   CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT, AI_AGENT):\n    pm health --check-only  ->  594 bytes\n    provenance_resolver_zero_success occurrences: 0\n\nCommitted baseline in scripts/release/token-budgets.json for health-default: baseline_bytes 549, baseline_estimated_tokens 138, max_bytes 604, max_estimated_tokens 152. Run B fits; run A does not.\n\nIndependence from this session's changes: git stash push -u followed by the gate on the resulting clean tree reproduces the same failure, so it is not caused by the working-tree diff.\n\nTrailing count 12 equals the number of items created, so the resolver is attempted once per mutation rather than once per session. The gate's own PM_AUTHOR override does not suppress the probe.\n\nWhy this is a recurrence rather than a new class: pm-xgah3a's first acceptance criterion required a sandboxed workspace to neutralize the harness signal environment so recorded provenance never depends on the process running the suite, and its resolution states it hardened sandboxes against only the ambiguous foreign AI_AGENT signal. pm-t7wn04's first two criteria required the token-budget gate's measured surfaces to be independent of ambient host state and required a negative control proving the same verdict on a runner and on a workstation for the same tree. Both are closed; both properties fail here today."
  "2026-08-16T13:26:31.120Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: the deterministic token gate now derives every supported built-in harness environment/model/session/provenance key from the SDK descriptor registry, removes those host-owned signals from its copied environment, preserves unrelated variables, and passed 24 focused tests plus the repository-wide 7,411-test exact-coverage gate. The live token gate passed all 32 surfaces, its 10,465-token unbounded negative control, and the infeasible-intent receipt."
  "2026-08-16T13:42:30.726Z","harness:codex","Reviewed-product lineage: implementation is published in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1042 at initial head f4ff1a393 and the PR body links this item on the GitHub-renderable main path."
